            <ArticleTitle>Epidural anaesthesia for caesarean section in pituitary dwarfism.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-124</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S2352-5568(16)30239-9</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.accpm.2016.02.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the anaesthetic management for caesarean section in a 32-year-old patient with pituitary dwarfism. In addition to supportive treatment, we offered a postoperative epidural analgesia pump. The patient recovered well without any complications.</AbstractText>
